T*
(* Principle: Absorption of IR radiation \(4,000 - 400 cm^-1\) excites molecular) Tj
T*
(vibrations \(stretching and bending\). Mandatory Selection Rule: A molecular vibration) Tj
T*
(is IR-active if and only if it produces a periodic change in the molecular dipole) Tj
T*
(moment: d\(mu\)/dq != 0. Homonuclear diatomics \(N2, O2, H2\) are IR-inactive;) Tj
T*
(heteronuclear molecules \(HCl, CO, CO2, H2O\) are IR-active.) Tj
T*
(* Hooke's Law for Vibrational Wave Number:) Tj
T*
(nu_bar = [ 1 / \(2 * pi * c\) ] * sqrt\( k / mu \),) Tj
T*
(where k = force constant of the chemical bond \(dyne/cm or N/m: k_single ~ 5*10^5,) Tj
T*
(k_double ~ 10*10^5, k_triple ~ 15*10^5 dyne/cm\), and mu = reduced mass = \(m1 * m2\) / \(m1) Tj
T*
(+ m2\).) Tj
T*
(* Characteristic IR Functional Group Regions:) Tj
T*
(- O-H / N-H stretching: 3,200 - 3,600 cm^-1 \(broad for hydrogen-bonded OH\).) Tj
T*
(- C-H stretching: 2,850 - 3,100 cm^-1.) Tj
T*
(- C#C / C#N \(Triple bond\) stretching: 2,100 - 2,260 cm^-1.) Tj
T*
(- C=O \(Carbonyl\) stretching: 1,650 - 1,750 cm^-1 \(very sharp and intense\).) Tj
T*
(- C=C \(Alkene/Aromatic\) stretching: 1,600 - 1,680 cm^-1.) Tj
T*
(- Fingerprint Region: 1,400 - 400 cm^-1 \(unique complex pattern for molecule) Tj
T*
(identification\).) Tj
