(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Two biochemical substances X and Y are present in a mixture. In a 1.0 cm cell) Tj
T*
(at lambda1 \(260 nm\): epsilon_X = 15,000 and epsilon_Y = 3,000 L/mol*cm. At lambda2 \(280) Tj
T*
(nm\): epsilon_X = 4,000 and epsilon_Y = 12,000 L/mol*cm. The mixture exhibits absorbances) Tj
T*
(of A_260 = 0.900 and A_280 = 0.800. Calculate concentrations C_X and C_Y.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Set Up Simultaneous Absorbance Equations:) Tj
T*
(At 260 nm: A_260 = \(15,000 * C_X\) + \(3,000 * C_Y\) = 0.900.) Tj
T*
(At 280 nm: A_280 = \(4,000 * C_X\) + \(12,000 * C_Y\) = 0.800.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Simplify Equations:) Tj
T*
(Divide Eq 1 by 3,000: 5 * C_X + C_Y = 0.000300 => C_Y = 0.000300 - 5 * C_X.) Tj
T*
(Divide Eq 2 by 4,000: C_X + 3 * C_Y = 0.000200.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Substitute C_Y into Eq 2:) Tj
T*
(C_X + 3 * \(0.000300 - 5 * C_X\) = 0.000200) Tj
T*
(C_X + 0.000900 - 15 * C_X = 0.000200 => -14 * C_X = -0.000700.) Tj
T*
(C_X = 0.000700 / 14 = 5.0 * 10^-5 M \(50 microM\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Solve for C_Y:) Tj
T*
(C_Y = 0.000300 - 5 * \(5.0 * 10^-5\) = 0.000300 - 0.000250 = 5.0 * 10^-5 M \(50 microM\).) Tj
T*
(Final Answer: C_X = 5.0 * 10^-5 M, C_Y = 5.0 * 10^-5 M.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
